From: Ryan Zegalia <ryanzegalia@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: qcs8550-ayn-thor: the lid wakes on both edges

pb-os 788b192 (from Armada) made the hall lid sensor wake only on the
lid-open edge (EV_ACT_DEASSERTED), so a lid closed on a Thor put to sleep
with the power key would not wake it. On our kernel that left a Thor put
to sleep with the lid open (power key or Steam's idle timer) unwakeable
by the lid at all: closed, then opened, nothing until the power key
(2026-10-20 13:53, battery, deep sleep).

Wake on any edge (EV_ACT_ANY, as ROCKNIX's Thor DT has it; gpio-keys then
keeps the line's both-edges trigger through suspend). A lid closed on a
sleeping Thor wakes it for a moment; a userspace helper on my Thor (not in this repo) sends it
straight back to deep sleep, now with the lid closed, from where opening
the lid wakes it. The pull-up (hall_lid_n) stays.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@
 			linux,input-type = <EV_SW>;
 			linux,code = <SW_LID>;
 			linux,can-disable;
-			wakeup-event-action = <EV_ACT_DEASSERTED>;
+			wakeup-event-action = <EV_ACT_ANY>;
 			wakeup-source;
 		};
 	};
